> I'm not really sure what you mean with "integrated device" and "other
> device". I've replaced the windows() function in my original script
> (which was working fine on the Windows machine) with the Mac-equivalent
> function quartz(). I thought I was doing the graphic work already "the
> standard way", am I not?

StatET/RJ provides an integrated graphic device called rj.gd. It is 
enabled by default, if you installed the R package 'rj.gd'. That means 
it is set as 'device' in the 'options' of R. To create a new plot using 
the default device you can use the R function 'dev.new'. The advantage 
of that function is, that your scripts work in any environment, it is 
only required that the default device is set to the desired device.

Regards,
Stephan


